  "text": {
    "intro": "The Ashfold Knitting Circle meets weekly and has not agreed on anything since 1998.\nFour knitters are involved. Determine each knitter's day, project and yarn.\n- **Knitter**: Ebba, Lionel, Angus and Maudie.\n- **Day** (listed from earlier to later): Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday and Thursday.\n- **Project**: a shawl of impossible lace, a fisherman's gansey, a cable-knit blanket and a Fair Isle tam.\n- **Yarn**: undyed Shetland, recycled sari silk, mohair of great expense and hand-spun alpaca.\nEvery knitter has a different day, project and yarn, so within each category every item is used exactly once.",
    "clues": [
      "The knitter who is making a cable-knit blanket knits on Wednesday.",
      "The knitter who is making a Fair Isle tam works in mohair of great expense.",
      "Wednesday is exactly one day earlier than the knitter who is making a shawl of impossible lace, with no day in between.",
      "Lionel does not knit on Wednesday.",
      "Maudie is exactly one day earlier than the knitter who works in mohair of great expense, with no day in between.",
      "Angus is not making a Fair Isle tam. The knitter who is making a Fair Isle tam is earlier than Lionel in day order.",
      "Angus does not work in recycled sari silk.",
      "The knitter who works in hand-spun alpaca is exactly one day earlier than the knitter who is making a Fair Isle tam, with no day in between."
    ]
  }
